    "reasoning": "The earlier selected options remain supported by each question's own captured worked solution. No submitted-answer grade was supplied. Fifteen questions have a unique mathematically correct listed choice. q-15178 has two correct choices: option 2 is MA's stated expression, while option 4 gives the same definite integral under u=\\pi/2-t. Thus its radio choices are mathematically nonunique, although MA's stated answer is correct. Calculations: q-47485 gives (0.03-0.015)/0.5=0.03 mi/s. q-126390 gives f'''(0)=6/16=3/8. q-142314 factors as (x+4)(x-3), so -4\\le x\\le3. q-10032 has horizontal width 1-y^3, giving area 3/4; the source's intermediate -3/4 is a signed integral, correctly converted to positive area at the end. q-78891 integrates 2\\cos y over [-\\pi/2,\\pi/2], giving 4. q-75121 gives (11-3)/0.8=10. q-47504 gives (6-(-10))/0.4=40 degrees per hour. q-15403 has derivative x^2\\sqrt{2x^3+1}, yielding arc-length radicand 2x^7+x^4+1. q-122389's selected curve has derivative -20x^3, whose square is 400x^6. q-15178 has speed \\sqrt{9\\sin^2t+4\\cos^2t}. q-123027 has squared speed 9\\sin^2t+(8-\\sin t)^2=10\\sin^2t-16\\sin t+64. q-30923 has antiderivative e^{x/3}, giving e-1. The polar questions use y'(\\theta)/x'(\\theta): q-141036 gives -\\cot(2\\theta); q-141040 gives (\\sin\\theta-\\cos\\theta)/(\\sin\\theta+\\cos\\theta); q-141048 gives -2/\\pi; q-142369 gives -\\cot(7\\pi/4)=1. General slope expressions apply wherever their denominators are nonzero.",
